<title>JAPAN: W.Australian Treasury Corp launches dual samurai.</title>
<headline>W.Australian Treasury Corp launches dual samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/U.S. dollar dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead-manager Nikko Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Western Australian Treasury Corp</p>
<p> AMT		 20 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    4.8 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  March 16, 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  Feb 28, 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Feb 17 to Feb 27</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>NOTE: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive US$4,028.68 for each 500,000 yen bond held at maturity. The bonds are guaranteed by the state of Western Australia. -- Tokyo Treasuries Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
